LinuxTerminal (formerly LinuxLab Hybrid) redistributes browser/runtime assets from third-party projects.

Third-party components include:
- v86 — x86 virtualization in the browser. See the upstream project and its license.
- xterm.js — terminal emulator components used by the browser UI.
- Monaco Editor — code editor components used by the learning simulator.
- SeaBIOS and VGABIOS — firmware assets used by the browser VM.
- Alpine Linux packages in the custom ISO — each package remains under its own upstream license; see the package inventory and license texts produced for each release.

